    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "PPO involves training a reward model on preference data, which consists of prompts, responses, and rankings. The reward model is then used to score model-generated responses during training. DPO, on the other hand, directly optimizes the policy model on preference data. <strong>The quality of the preference data and the choice of learning algorithm are crucial for downstream model performance</strong>.",
